{"abstract":[{"text":"Use your Apple Account to keep your LinkMap Projects available across your devices.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap","doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/iOS-Platform"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/iCloud"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"iCloud"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Get-ready-to-use-iCloud","level":2,"text":"Get ready to use iCloud","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"LinkMap for iOS uses the Apple Account signed in on your device. Make sure iCloud is available in Settings, then open LinkMap. You do not need a separate LinkMap account.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Projects you create are private until you share them. Shared Projects and Activities use their owner’s invitations and permissions; see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Sharing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"If-your-account-is-unavailable","level":2,"text":"If your account is unavailable","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Follow the message shown by LinkMap. Check your Apple Account in Settings and your network connection, then retry. If iCloud access is restricted on the device, resolve that restriction before continuing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A temporary network problem may still let you open locally available information. Reconnect when you need to load or save shared changes. Check any save error and retry before relying on a change being available to others.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Manage-your-data","level":2,"text":"Manage your data","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Manage Projects and their rec